{
  "dom_id": "step-q122047",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Given that $n\\ge 1$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(n-1)!}{(n+2)!}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n(n+2)!=(n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot n\\cdot (n-1)!\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $(n-1)!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n-1)!}{(n+2)!} & =\\frac{(n-1)!}{(n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot n\\cdot (n-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(n-1)!}}{(n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot n\\cdot \\cancel{(n-1)!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n(n+1)(n+2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
